  "body": "document.cookie currently uses the document URL for lookups in the cookie store -- see the [document.cookie spec](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/dom.html#dom-document-cookie). history.pushState and history.replaceState can be used to modify the document URL -- see step 10 in the [pushState/replaceState spec](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/history.html#dom-history-pushstate).\r\n\r\nIt follows that, according to the spec, a Web page can combine the two APIs to bypass cookie path scoping.\r\n\r\nThis was [raised on the Chromium bug tracker](https://crbug.com/782310), and the conclusion appears to be that document.cookie should be spec'd to use a cookies URL instead of the document URL. I think this would effectively codify Blink and WebKit's behavior into the spec. The same resolution seems to apply to #2641.",
